\documentclass{article}
\title{Stability of Mixed-Cation Perovskite Solar Cells}
\author{H. Lindqvist and P. Duarte}
\date{January 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Perovskite absorbers combine high absorption coefficients with long carrier diffusion lengths.
The empirical tolerance factor \alpha$ predicts whether a given cation mixture
crystallises into the desired photoactive phase at moderate annealing temperatures.
Films whose composition falls outside the stable window degrade within days
when they are exposed to humid air.
\end{document}

